[[Iacob II]] was the [[King of Burawa]] from 890 to 938. He was the son of [[Menag IV]] and the farther of [[Menag V]]. He ruled over Burawa during it's great [[Northern Conquest of Burawa]] that formed the modern borders of Burawa below the Kaftian mountain range.